{"name":"Orange Clay","hex":"#e6a57f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"clay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral substance made up of small crystals of silica and alumina, that is ductile when moist; the material of pre-fired ceramics.","An earth material with ductile qualities."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add clay to or to spread clay onto.","To purify using clay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay","wikidata":"Q42302"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 23,500 times magnified electron micrograph of smectite clay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClay_magnified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/500px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/1280px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg/500px-Italian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Italian and African-American clay miners in mine shaft, 1910","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AItalian_and_African-American_Clay_Miners_in_Mine_Shaft.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clay_In_A_Construction_Site.jpg/500px-Clay_In_A_Construction_Site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail